Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||09-05-2001||09:20 AM||||I have a problem.....<P><BR>My car craks over and over before it starts. This leads me to believe it's a relay. The oil pressure gauge goes up , whenit gets to about 1/2 it starts.<P>Now another problem I am having is the fuel pump is staying on , I don't know if this is related to the cranking , but I have a feeling it is.<P>I plugged in a new relay and the fuel pump came on ..and stayed on<P><BR>I have a 4hr trip tomorrow , I can drive the car with the problem , but would rather not.<P><BR>please help<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||09-05-2001||09:38 AM||||Sounds more like the oil pressure sensor is messed up. The oil pressure sensor controls the fuel pump also. It is suppose to keep the fuel pump on when you have pressure. (Switches the relay). It could be the sensor is stuck in one direction causing the relay to look bad.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||09-05-2001||10:14 AM||||where do I find this sensor?? hard to replace??<P><BR>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||09-05-2001||10:19 AM||||Is it a V-6 or a Duke?<BR>V-6 is located top right of the engine near the battery. It is on a pipe that goes to the oil filter below. It is between the valve cover and the battery. Not sure where it is located on the Duke.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-05-2001).]||||reg||1
